      "text": "## The Big Picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#002",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A properly designed, correctly sized, well-sealed duct system is the unsung variable\nin HVAC performance. Industry studies consistently find that typical existing US residential\nductwork leaks 20–30% of conditioned air into unconditioned attics and crawlspaces — energy\nwasted before it reaches any room. Equipment sizing and efficiency ratings are irrelevant\nif the distribution system defeats them."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#003",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    DUCT SYSTEM PERFORMANCE CHAIN                     |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Equipment    → Supply plenum → Supply trunk → Branch ducts → Rooms  |\n|  (designed     (pressurized)   (main artery)  (per room)   (delivery)|\n|  for 400 CFM/                                                        |\n|  ton airflow)                                                        |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Failure mode 1: Duct leakage → conditioned air into attic (lost)    |\n|  Failure mode 2: Undersized ducts → high static pressure → low flow  |\n|  Failure mode 3: Poorly designed → unbalanced delivery per room      |\n|  Failure mode 4: Compressed flex duct → massive pressure loss        |\n|                                                                      |\n|  Result: 3-ton equipment delivering 1.5-ton performance              |\n+----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
