      },
      "text": "## Section 1: Manual D — Duct Design Standard"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#006",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Duct design is a network flow allocation problem: pressure drop is proportional to flow rate times resistance; series resistances add; parallel branches share the pressure drop. The Manual D friction rate calculation allocates the available system pressure drop across a tree-structured duct network to achieve target airflow (CFM) at every leaf node (supply register) — structurally identical to sizing bandwidth in a hierarchical network topology or pipe diameters in a hydraulic distribution system."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#007",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Manual D (ACCA) is to ductwork what Manual J is to equipment sizing. Most residential\nduct systems in existing homes were not designed with Manual D. Most installers still\ndon't use it. This is why duct problems are epidemic."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#008",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  MANUAL D WORKFLOW:\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ INPUT: Manual J room-by-room loads + airflow requirements       │\n  │        Equipment specs (blower performance curve, TESP rating)  │\n  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             |\n                             v\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ CALCULATE: Available static pressure for ducts                  │\n  │  TESP available = Equipment fan capacity at design CFM          │\n  │  Minus: filter pressure drop (0.08–0.15\" w.c.)                  │\n  │  Minus: coil pressure drop (0.10–0.20\" w.c.)                    │\n  │  = Remaining for supply + return ductwork                       │\n  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             |\n                             v\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ FRICTION RATE: Pressure available / total effective length (TEL)│\n  │  TEL = straight duct length + equivalent lengths of all fittings│\n  │  Friction rate (FR) = inches w.c. per 100 ft                    │\n  │  Used to enter duct sizing chart → diameter per CFM per branch  │\n  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             |\n                             v\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ OUTPUT: Diameter of each duct run, sized to deliver Manual J    │\n  │         CFM to each room at acceptable velocity (<900 FPM)      │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
