      "text": "## Section 4: Duct Types and Materials"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#025",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  SHEET METAL (GALVANIZED STEEL):\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Best performance: smooth interior → lowest friction loss         │\n  │ Most durable: lasts decades                                      │\n  │ No compression degradation                                       │\n  │ Round or rectangular; fabricated to size                         │\n  │ Requires sheet metal shop or skilled fabrication                 │\n  │ Seams must be sealed with mastic or foil tape                    │\n  │ Most expensive; most labor-intensive                             │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#026",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "FLEX DUCT (INSULATED FLEXIBLE DUCT):\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Construction: wire helix (shape) + plastic inner liner +         │\n  │ fiberglass insulation (R-6 or R-8) + outer vapor barrier jacket  │\n  │                                                                  │\n  │ Advantages: easy to install around obstacles, lower cost         │\n  │                                                                  │\n  │ CRITICAL INSTALLATION REQUIREMENT:                               │\n  │ Must be FULLY EXTENDED — zero compression, no sag, no kinks      │\n  │                                                                  │\n  │ What installers often do:           What happens:                │\n  │ Leave slack in flex duct          →  Accordion compression       │\n  │ Drape over framing with sag       →  Low-point restriction       │\n  │ Route around obstacle with kink   →  Major pressure spike        │\n  │                                                                  │\n  │ 5% compression of flex duct → doubles pressure loss              │\n  │ 15% compression → 5× pressure loss                               │\n  │                                                                  │\n  │ Properly installed: only slightly worse than sheet metal         │\n  │ Improperly installed (common): massive airflow reduction         │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#027",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DUCT BOARD (FIBERGLASS DUCT BOARD):\n  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Rigid fiberglass panels fabricated into rectangular ductwork     │\n  │ Built-in insulation (no separate wrap needed)                    │\n  │ Slightly higher friction than sheet metal (rougher interior)     │\n  │ Requires sealing at all joints (mastic or foil tape)             │\n  │ Cannot handle high static pressure applications                  │\n  │ Common in light commercial; some residential                     │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
