      "text": "## Section 5: Duct Sealing"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#030",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Duct leakage is one of the highest-return improvements possible in existing homes.\nA 3-ton unit leaking 25% of supply air into the attic is operating like a 2.25-ton unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#031",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  SEALING METHODS:\n  ┌─────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ Mastic sealant  │ Gray paste applied with brush; dries flexible  │\n  │ (recommended)   │ Best for: rigid duct seams, boot connections,  │\n  │                 │ register boxes; permanent; code-approved       │\n  ├─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Metal (foil)    │ Aluminum foil tape with aggressive adhesive    │\n  │ tape, UL181-    │ (UL181B-FX listed — not generic hardware tape) │\n  │ rated           │ Good for: clean metal-to-metal connections     │\n  │                 │ Will fail if applied over dust/dirt            │\n  ├─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ \"Duct tape\"     │ NEVER use gray fabric duct tape for ductwork   │\n  │ (DO NOT USE)    │ Fails at temperature cycling in <5 years       │\n  │                 │ Not code-compliant; adhesive melts             │\n  ├─────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Aeroseal        │ Spray-from-inside polymer sealing method       │\n  │ (injection)     │ System is pressurized; particles blown through │\n  │                 │ leaks → accumulate → seal from inside         │\n  │                 │ Ideal for: inaccessible attic/crawlspace ducts │\n  │                 │ Can seal holes up to ~5/8\" diameter            │\n  │                 │ Professional installation required ($1,500–3k) │\n  └─────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#032",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "LEAKAGE TESTING — DUCT BLASTER:\n  Similar principle to blower door but for duct system\n  - Connect to return plenum; seal supply registers\n  - Pressurize to 25 Pa; measure CFM25 (airflow at 25 Pa)\n  - Compare to floor area → CFM25/100 sq ft"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#033",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STANDARDS:\n  IECC new construction:  ≤ 4 CFM25/100 sq ft total leakage\n  Energy Star:             ≤ 3 CFM25/100 sq ft to outside\n  Passive House:           essentially zero leakage (no ducts preferred)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#034",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Total leakage vs. leakage to outside:\n  - Total: all duct leaks including inside conditioned space (less harmful)\n  - To outside: only leaks to unconditioned space (attic, crawl, garage)\n  - \"To outside\" is what actually wastes energy; the harder metric\n```"
    },
