      "text": "## Section 6: Supply and Return Balance"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#037",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
        "canonical_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "current_path": "hvac/07-DUCTWORK.md",
        "id": "maxim:hvac:ductwork",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "hvac",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[ductwork]",
        "section": "hvac",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Ductwork",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  COMMON INSTALLER SHORTCUT: central return only\n  - Single large return at hallway; no return in bedrooms\n  - Result: closed bedroom door = no airflow path\n  → Bedroom becomes positive pressure (supply air, no return)\n  → Hallway becomes negative pressure\n  → Pressure difference = 3–5 Pa across door\n  → Building now operates like an exhaust-only ventilation system\n  → Duct leakage to outdoors dramatically increases (pressure drives it)"
    },
    {
      "id": "07-DUCTWORK.md#038",
      "path": [
        "07-DUCTWORK.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:hvac:07-ductwork, git-history:hvac:07-ductwork]",
